# Typography: First line indent, positive for paragraphs and negative for a hanging indent.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · First line indent
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: indented
			Box:
				Margin: 0
			Typography:
				First line indent: 18
				Align: justify
		For style: clause
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 8 0
				Padding: 0 0 0 60
			Typography:
				First line indent: -60
				Markup: markdown
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: First line indent
		Paragraph: `First line indent` starts the first line of a paragraph later. With a negative value the first line starts before the others, in the left `Padding` of the box: the hanging indent of clauses, bibliographies and glossaries.
			Style: intro
		Text: First line indent: 18  (paragraphs without a gap between them)
			Style: label
		Block:
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 20 0
			Paragraph: The first paragraph of the chapter starts after a short indent, like the following ones. The indent tells the paragraphs apart without leaving a blank line between them.
				Style: indented
			Paragraph: Only the first line of each paragraph is indented. The rest of the lines start at the left edge of the box, and a justified paragraph is aligned in what is left of the first line.
				Style: indented
			Paragraph: A paragraph that goes on in another page or column does not indent the first line of its second part.
				Style: indented
		Text: First line indent: -60 with Padding: 0 0 0 60  (a hanging indent)
			Style: label
		Paragraph: **FIRST.** The landlord grants the tenant the use of the dwelling, which the tenant uses as a main residence, with the furniture listed in the inventory.
			Style: clause
		Paragraph: **SECOND.** The term is one year from the signing of this contract, renewable by tacit agreement for periods of equal length.
			Style: clause
		Paragraph: **THIRD.** The rent is paid in the first five days of each month, by transfer to the account of the landlord.
			Style: clause
